<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Details on measuring FADE with text-to-image diffusion models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide details on computing FADE with text-to-image diffusion models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rombach et al., 2022</a>)</cite>. We assume the model to follow the Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Model (DDPM) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al., 2020</a>)</cite>, as used in the UnlearnCanvas <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>. For completeness, we provide background information on DDPM first, then derive the approximation on the log-likelihood difference term in FADE using denoising losses of the two models as proxies.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Model</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">DDPM defines a generative model by reversing a fixed forward diffusion process. The forward process gradually corrupts data with Gaussian noise over a sequence of timesteps, while the reverse process is parameterized by a neural network trained to denoise and recover the data distribution.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Forward Process.</span>   Given a data sample <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}\sim q({\bm{x}}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, the forward diffusion process produces a sequence of latent variables <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\bm{x}}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\bm{x}}_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> by progressively adding Gaussian noise:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t};\sqrt{1-\beta_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t-1},\beta_{t}{\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t-1})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t};\sqrt{1-\beta_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{t-1},\beta_{t}{\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is a fixed variance schedule given as a hyperparameter and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the identity matrix. Defining <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}=1-\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}=1-\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\alpha_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\prod_{s=1}^{t}\alpha_{s}</annotation></semantics></math>, one can express <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> an arbitrary timestep <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in closed form as:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t};\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{0},(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}){\bm{I}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle q({\bm{x}}_{t}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t};\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{0},(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}){\bm{I}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This formulation allows sampling <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> directly from <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> without iterating through all previous steps one-by-one.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Reverse Process.</span>   The generative model learns to approximate the reverse denoising process,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t-1};\bm{\mu}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t),\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t})=\mathcal{N}({\bm{x}}_{t-1};\bm{\mu}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t),\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t},t))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the mean <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is parameterized as a neural network and variance <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> is either fixed or learned. Since <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is given as input, a common parameterization is to train the network to predict the noise <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> added in the forward process instead, enabling reparameterization of <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Objective.</span>   Training DDPM minimizes a variational bound on the negative log-likelihood, which reduces to the denoising mean squared error (MSE) loss from predicting the injected noise <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> given the noised image <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t}\coloneqq\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t}\coloneqq\sqrt{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{x}}_{0}+\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\bm{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}},t}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\text{MSE}}({\bm{\epsilon}},{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t))\right]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}},t}\left[\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>MSE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}},t}\left[\mathcal{L}_{\text{MSE}}({\bm{\epsilon}},{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t))\right]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}},t}\left[\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Derivation of Approximating FADE</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During derivation of the denoising MSE loss in DDPM, the authors observe that the variational bound is decomposed into three terms (Equation 5 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho et al. (2020)</a></cite>):</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A1.Ex8.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:59.3pt;vertical-align:-39.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(123.2pt,-18.4pt) scale(2.63028381375753,2.63028381375753) ;">
<p id="A1.Ex8.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})]\leq\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid\mid p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{T}))}_{L_{T}}+\sum_{t&gt;1}\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid\mid p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}))}_{L_{t-1}}\underbrace{-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1})}_{L_{0}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></munder><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∣</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0})]\leq\mathbb{E}_{q}\left[\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{T}\mid{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid\mid p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{T}))}_{L_{T}}+\sum_{t&gt;1}\underbrace{D_{\text{KL}}(q({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t},{\bm{x}}_{0})\mid\mid p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{t-1}\mid{\bm{x}}_{t}))}_{L_{t-1}}\underbrace{-\log p_{\theta}({\bm{x}}_{0}\mid{\bm{x}}_{1})}_{L_{0}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here, <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant assuming the the noise scheduling <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}_{t=1}^{T}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> is not implemented as part of the model: the denoising loss is derived from <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math> terms only, following</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L_{t-1}+C=\gamma_{t}\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t))\|" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{t-1}+C=\gamma_{t}\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{\theta}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t))\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}=\frac{\beta_{t}^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}\alpha_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}=\frac{\beta_{t}^{2}}{2\sigma_{t}^{2}\alpha_{t}(1-\bar{\alpha}_{t})}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{t}^{2}=\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{t}^{2}=\frac{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t-1}}{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant independent of the parameters.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Derivation.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the denoiser from the retain-only and unlearned diffusion models. Additionally, let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{r}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{r}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{r}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{r}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{r}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{r}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the three components in the variational bound for the retain model (<math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{u}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{u}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{u}_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{u}_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{u}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{u}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> similarly for the unlearned model). As the two models are parameterized identically and are trained largely on identical data, we assume (1) that the variational gap between the negative log-likelihood and the variational bound is similar between the two models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cremer et al., 2018</a>)</cite> and (2) the difference between <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}^{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>r</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}^{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{0}^{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>u</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{0}^{u}</annotation></semantics></math> is small. Using the two assumptions and <a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ A.2 Derivation of Approximating FADE ‣ Appendix A Details on measuring FADE with text-to-image diffusion models ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 1</span></a> leads to</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center">
<div id="A1.Ex9.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_markedasmath ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:25.2pt;vertical-align:-16.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(20.8pt,-1.3pt) scale(1.11698457794383,1.11698457794383) ;">
<p id="A1.Ex9.1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\left[-\log\dfrac{p_{r}({\bm{x}}_{0})}{p_{u}({\bm{x}}_{0})}\right]\approx\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t&gt;1}(L_{t-1}^{r}-L_{t-1}^{u})\right]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}}}\left[\sum_{t&gt;1}\gamma_{t}\left(\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|-\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|\right)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>u</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0}}\left[-\log\dfrac{p_{r}({\bm{x}}_{0})}{p_{u}({\bm{x}}_{0})}\right]\approx\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{t&gt;1}(L_{t-1}^{r}-L_{t-1}^{u})\right]=\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{x}}_{0},{\bm{\epsilon}}}\left[\sum_{t&gt;1}\gamma_{t}\left(\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|-\|{\bm{\epsilon}}-{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}(\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t},t)\|\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</span></div></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In other words, the difference in log-likelihoods of a data point <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> can be approximated by a weighted sum of the differences in MSE losses obtained by forwarding the same perturbed inputs <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{x}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\epsilon}}_{u}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional Experimental Results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Full quantitative results from TOFU</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ B.1 Full quantitative results from TOFU ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 7</span></a> shows FADE measurements fromt he TOFU benchmark across all LoRA ranks in {4,8,16,32} and forget set splits TOFU-{1,5,10}%. Similarly, <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ B.1 Full quantitative results from TOFU ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure 8</span></a> shows the corresponding results, but using the forget quality and model utility metrics originally used in the TOFU benchmark. We find that in terms of forget quality, most methods improve significantly, a trend that can lead to misleading conclusions unless evaluated at a distributional level using FADE.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.12981v1/full_fade_results_eval_log_forget.svg" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/276;" width="548" height="276"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>FADE measurements (y-axis in log-scale; lower is better) across 5 unlearning epochs (x-axis) against each corresponding retain model on the TOFU benchmark. The dashed line represents a baseline value of FADE due to randomness in initialization and training (measured across 3 different seeds). The shaded regions indicate the standard deviation across 3 random seeds.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.12981v1/fade_tofu_results_all_ranks_tight.svg" id="A2.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/263;" width="548" height="263"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Quantitative results from TOFU based on the Forget Quality (FQ) and Model Utility (MU) metrics originally used in the TOFU benchmark. A higher value is better for both FQ and MU, and an ideal unlearning trajectory should start from the pretrained base model (<math id="A2.F8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\blacksquare" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">■</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\blacksquare</annotation></semantics></math>) and head towards the retain-only oracle (<math id="A2.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigstar" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">★</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigstar</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="A2.F8.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">.</p></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Text response examples from TOFU</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ B.2 Text response examples from TOFU ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 4</span></a>shows additional examples generated by a retain model, alongside NLL assignments of other retain models trained with a different seed and various unlearned models (analogous to <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 LLM Unlearning Results from TOFU ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 1</span></a>). While there are small variations in the NLL values from the retain models depending on the question under concern, the unlearned models assign much smaller likelihoods (larger NLL) overall to the responses from the retain model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ B.2 Text response examples from TOFU ‣ Appendix B Additional Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 5</span></a>shows additional textual examples generated from models unlearned using each method for 5 epochs with LoRA rank 32 (analogous to <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5.1 LLM Unlearning Results from TOFU ‣ 5 Experimental Results ‣ Reference-Specific Unlearning Metrics Can Hide the Truth: A Reality Check" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table 2</span></a>. We find that the behavior of GA, GD, and IHL collapsing to repeating the same tokens is shown consistently across various prompts. On the other hand, NPO generates unrelated gibberish that the unlearned model itself assigns low likelihood, and the retain model assigns an even lower likelihood. Lastly, DPO consistenly outputs refusal answers that the retain model is unlikely to generate.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Additional examples of top-10 most likely answers generated by a retain-only model to questions in TOFU-10%. The NLL assigned by other retain models (with different seeds) and unlearned models are shown to the right. Each group of responses and NLL values are obtained from prompting the question indicated on top of each section.</figcaption>
<div id="A2.T4.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:388.6pt;vertical-align:-193.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-406.7pt,397.5pt) scale(0.328283470043255,0.328283470043255) ;">
